WEBVTT

NOTE
Canonical written narration timed from the exact local narration render receipt.
Pronunciation-only substitutions are intentionally absent from caption text.

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.791
This chapter asks a specific question: An AI system can preserve

2
00:00:05.791 --> 00:00:09.959
internal evidence discipline and still change beliefs, choices,

3
00:00:09.959 --> 00:00:15.690
and institutions through selective framing, personalization, synthetic identity, repetition, and amplification.

4
00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:20.891
The stack therefore needs an owner for the complete outbound communication

5
00:00:20.891 --> 00:00:25.310
transaction, including correction after a message escapes its original channel.

6
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:30.484
The tempting shortcut is insufficient: Truthfulness checks, content filters,

7
00:00:30.484 --> 00:00:35.855
generic human-factors guidance, and red-team prompts inspect fragments of influence.

8
00:00:36.195 --> 00:00:41.982
They do not bind the claim, evidence ceiling, audience, vulnerability, purpose,

9
00:00:41.982 --> 00:00:47.243
personalization inputs, persuasive technique, channel, amplification, observed effect, correction, retraction,

10
00:00:47.243 --> 00:00:50.400
and remedy into one governed lifecycle.

11
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.572
The chapter's core claim is this: Consequential AI communication should be

12
00:00:56.572 --> 00:01:02.145
eligible for delivery only through an evidence-bounded communication packet whose audience,

13
00:01:02.145 --> 00:01:06.197
influence method, amplification authority, provenance, expiry, correction reach,

14
00:01:06.197 --> 00:01:08.730
and observed effects remain inspectable;

15
00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:14.979
fluent text, factual fragments, user consent, or a successful persuasion score

16
00:01:14.979 --> 00:01:19.813
alone establishes neither epistemic safety, autonomy, legitimacy, durable benefit,

17
00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:21.425
nor release readiness.

18
00:01:21.765 --> 00:01:27.933
Compile a communication packet from claim identity, maximum warranted inference, uncertainty,

19
00:01:27.933 --> 00:01:34.102
audience class, purpose, protected or denied personalization attributes, persuasive technique, channel,

20
00:01:34.102 --> 00:01:40.270
disclosure, and amplification ceiling. Run audience-risk and autonomy checks before delivery.

21
00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:46.095
Vulnerability, dependency, power asymmetry, urgency, and inability to exit narrow the

22
00:01:46.095 --> 00:01:48.090
permitted technique and scale.

23
00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:52.720
A concrete implementation trace makes the proposal testable.

24
00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:59.426
A useful first implementation is a communication-packet schema plus a delivery

25
00:01:59.426 --> 00:02:05.792
proxy that rejects evidence overstatement, denied personalization, undisclosed sponsorship, unbounded amplification,

26
00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:09.265
missing expiry, and unreachable correction routes.

27
00:02:09.605 --> 00:02:14.969
A benign held-out study can compare neutral assistance, bounded personalization, disclosure,

28
00:02:14.969 --> 00:02:20.333
and correction variants while measuring comprehension and autonomy as well as

29
00:02:20.333 --> 00:02:25.697
persuasion. It must not optimize vulnerable users or treat short-horizon self-report

30
00:02:25.697 --> 00:02:27.160
as durable welfare.

31
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:33.203
Run audience-risk and autonomy checks before delivery. Vulnerability, dependency, power asymmetry,

32
00:02:33.203 --> 00:02:38.905
urgency, and inability to exit narrow the permitted technique and scale.

33
00:02:39.505 --> 00:02:45.158
The design can still fail. calibrated-sounding misinformation selective framing sycophancy emotional

34
00:02:45.158 --> 00:02:50.296
manipulation The correct response is to stop, narrow, quarantine, compensate,

35
00:02:50.296 --> 00:02:55.435
or retain an owned residual rather than narrate uncertainty away.

36
00:02:56.035 --> 00:03:01.081
This chapter remains Design rationale at argument support. Its contracts, examples,

37
00:03:01.081 --> 00:03:05.210
tests, or local artifacts establish only their encoded scope.

38
00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:10.256
The chapter names proof targets rather than pretending they are already

39
00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:10.715
closed.

40
00:03:11.055 --> 00:03:16.462
A finite Human-AI Communication, Persuasion, and Epistemic Security record may hand

41
00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:20.395
off only when identity, authority, version, required checks,

42
00:03:20.395 --> 00:03:25.802
and residual ownership are present; no theorem grants empirical effectiveness or

43
00:03:25.802 --> 00:03:26.785
release authority.

44
00:03:27.125 --> 00:03:33.109
Personalization may not use denied attributes or exploit a known vulnerability.

45
00:03:33.109 --> 00:03:38.005
Amplification requires a bounded audience denominator and revocable authority.

46
00:03:38.605 --> 00:03:43.569
No chapter claim or evidence state is promoted by this visual.

47
00:03:43.569 --> 00:03:48.533
A named mechanism is not proof of correct implementation or useful

48
00:03:48.533 --> 00:03:53.497
deployment. A local check or formal model does not establish real-world

49
00:03:53.497 --> 00:03:58.010
